<h2 class="design">Rattlesnakes, Mass Murderers and A Pool-Shooting Hermit</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">Who Is Cormac McCarthy?</h4>

<p>

The last (and only?) interview <a href="http://www.cormacmccarthy.com">Cormac McCarthy</a> did was <a href="http://www.nytimes.com/books/98/05/17/specials/mccarthy-venom.html">this one,</a> for the New York Times Magazine, in 1992.<br />
<br />
But <a href="http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/sptimes/445483311.html?MAC=1cdb755671586fa0bfb17e62e9426fe1&did=445483311&FMT=FT&FMTS=FT&date=Nov+13%2C+2003&author=KELLEY+BENHAM&pub=St.+Petersburg+Times&printformat=&desc=A+THOUSAND+WORDS+ABOUT+THE+TERRI+SCHIAVO+YOU+NEVER+KNEW">someone</a> has been thinking lately about how cool it would be to talk to the lonesome genius who wrote: <br />
<br />
They rode. You ever get ill at ease? said Rawlins. About what? I dont know. About anything. Just ill at ease. Sometimes. If you're someplace you aint supposed to be I guess you'd be ill at ease. Should be anyways. Well suppose you were ill at ease and didnt know why. Would that mean that you might be someplace you wasn't supposed to be and didnt know it? What the hell's wrong with you? I dont know. Nothin. I believe I'll sing. He did.
